---
import SiteFrame from "../components/SiteFrame.astro";
---

<SiteFrame
  title="Telemetry · ClickHouse Loom"
  description="What self-hosted Loom reports and how to control sharing."
  path="/telemetry"
>
  <h1>Telemetry</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Self-hosted Loom reports aggregate usage so we can see which features people use
    and how installations adopt them.
  </p>
  <div class="details">
    <section>
      <h2>What Loom sends</h2>
      <p>
        Every completed 12-hour window can produce one report with an installation identifier,
        software versions, and counts of requests, feature usage, namespaces, agents, and sessions.
        The report contains no customer content, full email addresses, or credentials.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        The server sends reports over HTTPS to <code>loom.clickhouse.com/api/v1/adoption</code>.
        Reports are retained for 400 days.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Control sharing</h2>
      <p>Set this on every server and worker replica to disable adoption reports.</p>
      <pre><code>LOOM_ADOPTION_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false</code></pre>
      <p>Verified email domains, account counts, and the number of successful requests in their verified namespaces are shared only when an operator enables domain sharing.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <a href="/docs/features/observability/telemetry#self-hosted-adoption">Read the telemetry field reference</a>
</SiteFrame>

<style>
  .details { max-width: 43rem; margin-block: 2.5rem; }
  section { padding-block: 1.35rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  section p { margin-top: 0.6rem; }
  code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  pre { background: #20201b; padding: 1rem; overflow: auto; border-radius: 0.35rem; }
  main > a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
